  "title": "Ph Insurance Faqs Objections — FAQ 1: How does premium payment work and what happens if I miss a due date?",
  "content": "### FAQ 1: How does premium payment work and what happens if I miss a due date?\n- **Answer**: Premiums can be paid monthly, quarterly, semi-annually, or annually via bank auto-debit (BDO, BPI, Metrobank, Security Bank), online banking, GCash, or Maya. Every policy includes a statutory 31-day grace period. If you miss a payment, your coverage remains 100% active during those 31 days. If unpaid after 31 days without cash value, the policy lapses, but you can reinstate it within three years.",
  "context_header": "[Document: ph_insurance_faqs_objections.md] [Product: Philippines Life Insurance] [Category: faq] [Section: FAQ 1: How does premium payment work and what happens if I miss a due date?]",
